-- People P3-C1 (docs/people-leave-p3c-ledger-architecture.md §C, §I.2a, §I.3, §J.1, §J.2, §L): the leave
-- balance ledger core. Generated by `prisma migrate diff`, then the constraints, guards, stage gate,
-- deferred invariants, partial unique indexes, grants, restrictive read policies and the revision
-- effective_from back-fill that Prisma cannot express were added by hand (section marked "hand-written").
-- One transaction (docs/migration-readiness.md §7): a failure leaves nothing behind.
--
-- Ordering: depends on 20261204000000_people_leave_policies (leave types, policies, revisions) and
-- 20261118000000_people (employees). It sorts after every stamp on main (newest 20261207000000_workflow_links)
-- and in open PRs at build time (newest 20261210000000_sales_configuration, PR #135); it depends on neither.
-- No privileged SQL, no extension.
--
-- Class: additive DDL (five new, empty tables) PLUS an existing-data transformation of
-- people_leave_policy_revisions (two new columns, back-filled; §J.2). Not routine: needs the J.2 preflight,
-- a rehearsal on a disposable branch and lock limits before any production apply (docs/people-leave-p3c1.md).
--
-- Disabled by default: no route, no engine, no job. The stage gate accepts only the derived transaction
-- kinds (ACCRUAL, YEAR_OPEN, CONSUME, FREEZE, CARRY_PROPAGATION); every request and manual kind, WRITE_OFF,
-- POLICY_EXPIRY, DAYS-unit postings and every correction authorisation are refused until the package that
-- adds their backstop (C3/B2, C5, D-P3C-11, D-P3C-15, the revised D-P3C-23).
--
-- SQLSTATEs (class PE, people; PE001-PE012 are P1's and P3-A's; P3-B numbers after these):
--   PE013 ledger rows are immutable (UPDATE of a transaction or entry; identity of an account or bucket)
--   PE014 the writer does not hold the account lock (the account version was not bumped in this transaction)
--   PE015 not enabled in this stage (request/manual kinds, WRITE_OFF, POLICY_EXPIRY, DAYS basis, authorisations)
--   PE016 ledger rule (kind/basis matrix, book/sign, bucket state, dates, references, idempotency key shape)
--   PE017 ledger invariant at commit (pairs, settlement, year closing, lapse, sensitivity containment, empty)
--   PE018 leave_reference_not_visible: a cited row exists but the writer cannot read it (D-P3C-37 (a))
--   PE019 the writer may not post here (no app.user_id, no business date, or cannot read the whole account)
--   (PE009 stale is reused for a version that does not advance by exactly one.)
BEGIN;
-- Fail fast instead of queueing. The back-fill (end of file) takes ACCESS EXCLUSIVE on businesses and
-- people_leave_policy_revisions until COMMIT, so it runs last and every statement is bounded.
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '3s';
SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '30s';


-- AlterTable
ALTER TABLE "people_leave_policy_revisions" ADD COLUMN     "effective_from" DATE,
ADD COLUMN     "effective_from_basis" TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'RECORDED';

